@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_Path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Disclosure}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview_Tests}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Disclosure @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview_Tests</PageTitle>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class @GlobalValues.Info_Box_Coloured_Modifier">
    <h1 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Disclosure @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview_Tests</h1>

    <p>
        A disclosure is a simple component that shows or hides its content on activating its triggering element.
    </p>
    <p>
        <b>Released: </b>Current version <b>v1.0.0</b> See the documentation site for more information: <a target="_blank" class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@GlobalValues.Site_Link_Docs_Disclosure">Disclosure documentation (opens in new window)</a>
    </p>
</section>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h2 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Information & instructions</h2>
    <p>
        Below is a single Disclosure component which, in this instance has been configured with a maximum content height of 40vh (viewpoint height units). This is proportionate to the window size and as such 
        if its not large enough for the content a vertical scrollbar will appear. You can adjust the window to make the scrollbar appear/disappear.
    </p>
    <p>
        Using the keys as described below, navigate to the disclosure ensuring you can expand and collapse it to read its content.
    </p>
    <p>
        Change the page size so a scrollbar appears, using only a keyboard try to scroll the content.
    </p>
    <h2 id="disclosure-keyboard" class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Keyboard interaction</h2>
    <ul aria-labelledby="disclosure-keyboard">
        <li>
            <kbd>Tab</kbd> - places focus on the trigger button. When the content is expanded, focus then moves through any focusable elements inside it, or onto the content
            itself if it scrolls and has nothing focusable inside.
        </li>

        <li><kbd>Space or Enter</kbd> - when on the trigger, expands or collapses the content..</li>
        <li>
            <kbd>Arrow keys</kbd> - <kbd>Page Up, Page Down</kbd> - <kbd>Home, End</kbd> when a scrollable content region has focus, scroll it using the browser's standard behaviour.
        </li>
    </ul>

</section>
<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class">

    <h3 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Expectations</h3>

    <ul>
        <li>
            Tabbing to the disclosure component should set focus on the triggering element (button).
        </li>
        <li>
            Using the enter or space key should expand or collapse the disclosure. Screen reader users should be advised of the state, expanded/collapsed.
        </li>
        <li>
            Keyboard-only users should be able to tab to the content area when there is a scrollbar and be able to scroll the content. Screen reader users
            should be advised that this stop is for a group, with the name of the triggering element ("Lorem ipsum text in a disclosure") -but only when there
            is a scrollbar.
        </li>
        <li>
            Voice control users should be able to navigate, expand or collapse the disclosure by using the visible accessible name with the associated command.
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="section-box">
    <h3>Disclosure test</h3>

